# Render API service (start command: ./start.sh api). Names only; never commit values.
# Copy to .env.render.api (gitignored), fill in, then paste it into the service's
# Environment page with "Add from .env". Leave RENDER, VERA_PUBLIC_MODE and VERA_TRUST_PROXY unset.
# NOT needed, and must NOT be set, for the zero-spend deployment: config/ask-provider-chain.json ships
# openai_fallback.enabled=false, so the API never calls OpenAI. Set it only if that switch is changed to true (paid route).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Strong random key; the same value goes in .env.render.ui.
VERA_API_KEY=
# Optional, free-tier-first /ask (item #77): with this set, /ask is answered by Groq at $0; OpenAI is a
# fallback only if openai_fallback.enabled is true (shipped false). Providers and models: config/ask-provider-chain.json.
GROQ_API_KEY=
# Optional, only after adding an OpenRouter entry to config/ask-provider-chain.json (see its openrouter_example).
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# REQUIRED (VERA_DB_URL_RO) for DAR and full-document reads (also feeds the corpus description in the sidebar, item #83): Render's INTERNAL database URL with the READ-ONLY
# account, e.g. <ro-db-url>. This is the only database variable offered for the Render API.
# Unset = DAR/full-document reads unavailable and "description not available". Name is read via config/ask-provider-chain.json (read_db_url_env).
# VERA_DB_URL_RO=
# Full-document answers read from the database (DB-backed reader, vera/fulldoc_db.py): the run id is not a secret. Set ONLY after the
# DB-backed answering is approved; unset = reader off (reading-list mode). The reader uses VERA_DB_URL_RO above, no other DB variable.
# VERA_FULLDOC_DB_RUN_ID=
# Database access on Render is read-only. Do NOT set VERA_DB_URL_WO, VERA_DB_URL_RW, VERA_DB_URL_ADMIN or
# DATABASE_URL on the Render API service. Corpus growth (item #79 phase C) therefore stays off there
# (unset = sources are not stored).
